T0090 "Nine of fifteen deps unpinned, two bypass system-first" is now CLOSED.

Evidence from cmake/Dependencies.cmake (grep 2026-11-11):
  - All four CPMAddPackage calls pin GIT_TAG to full 40-char commit SHAs:
      fmt               0c9fce2ffefecfdce794e1859584e25877b7b592
      spdlog            27cb4c76708608465c413f6d0e6b8d99a4d84302
      tomlplusplus      30172438cee64926dc41fdd9c11fb3ba5b2ba9de
      readerwriterqueue 8e7627d18c2108aca178888d88514179899a044f
    None tracks a mutable tag. (The 2026-10-23 tag->commit swap below is now
    also build-verified: the hash-pinned CPM bootstrap cold-configured with
    EXIT 0 today, STATUS/T0089.log.)
  - pffft, one of the two dependencies that bypassed the system-first
    find_package-then-CPM-fallback policy, was removed 2026-10-04. Only
    readerwriterqueue remains an unconditional CPMAddPackage; it is header-only
    with no system package to prefer, so a system-first probe would be vacuous.
  - The other historical OPEN item, "CPM_SOURCE_CACHE defaults OFF", is FIXED:
    it now defaults to <source>/.cpm-cache, shared across all build profiles.
  - The remaining "unpinned" inputs are host system packages (Qt6, OpenGL,
    TagLib, glm, FFmpeg's five components, libavfilter, projectM) found by
    find_package / pkg-config, with a 6.8 version floor on Qt. A system
    package's version is whatever the host ships; it is not commit-pinnable and
    is not something CPM or Conan would replace.

So every actionable half of the task ("pin CPM tags", "stop bypassing
system-first", "share the cache") is done. docs/dev/DEPENDENCIES.md's
"Why not Conan" section still claimed nine unpinned deps and a missing
vcpkg.json (T0091, long done); corrected in the same commit. Genuinely
remaining reproducibility work is tracked separately: T0301 (SBOM /
dependency-vulnerability lane), T0338 (Windows vcpkg port pinning).

